          %p
            %br/
          %h3#octonionic_construction_of_representations Octonionic construction of representations
          %p
            The group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8)
            has three 8-dimensional irreducible real representations: the right- and left-handed spinor representations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_+
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_-
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 8
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(8)
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Bryant20"} Bryant 20
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonions"} octonions
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝕆
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathbb{O}
            define a linear map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕆
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕆
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_x \colon \mathbb{O}^2 \to \mathbb{O}^2
            as follows:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %msub
                            %mi R
                            %mi x
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi C
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_x = \left( \begin{array}{cc} 0 &amp; C R_x \\ -C L_x &amp; 0  \end{array}   \right)
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝕆
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝕆
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_x, R_x, C \colon \mathbb{O} \to \mathbb{O}
            are left multiplication by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and octonionic conjugation, respectively. Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi m
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_x^2 = -{|x|}^2
            this map induces an action of the Clifford algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cliff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕆
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cliff(\mathbb{O})
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕆
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{O}^2
            %em minus
            1). One can show that this action gives an isomorphism of real associative algebras
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cliff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕆
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi End
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕆
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cliff(\mathbb{O}) \cong End(\mathbb{O}^2)
          %p
            where
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi End
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕆
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} End(\mathbb{O}^2)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕆
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{O}^2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 16
                  %mo ×
                  %mn 16
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 16 \times 16
            real matrices.
          %p
            The group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8)
            is isomorphic to the group of linear transformations generated by products
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_x m_y
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝕆
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in \mathbb{O}
            have
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|x|} = {|y|} = 1
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mi u
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi R
                            %mi u
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left( \begin{array}{cc} L_u &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; R_u \end{array}   \right)
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝕆
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \in \mathbb{O}
            has
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|u|} = 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8)
            is generated by unit octonions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
          %p
            It follows that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕆
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{O}^2
            splits, as a representation of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 8
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕆
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{O}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 8
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            acts as
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_u
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            acts as
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_u
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_+
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8)
            can also be identified with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕆
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{O}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            acting as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi u
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_u R_u
          %p
            Bryant also describes the intertwiners
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mo ±
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∓
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes S_{\pm} \to S_{\mp}
            and the triality automorphisms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(8)
            in these terms.
